                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The codecs that were added in AVRO-957 (zlib and lzma) are optional.  However, if you compile the C library with the required libraries being present, you get an invalid pkgconfig file:<br/>
<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
$ cat src/avro-c.pc<br/>
Name: avro-c<br/>
Description: C library for parsing Avro data<br/>
Version: 1.6.2-SNAPSHOT<br/>
URL: http://avro.apache.org/<br/>
Libs: -L/usr/local/Cellar/avro-c/HEAD/lib -lavro<br/>
Cflags: -I/usr/local/Cellar/avro-c/HEAD/include<br/>
Requires: zlib @LZMA_PKG@<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
(The @LZMA_PKG@ part is a substitution variable that wasn&#39;t substituted.)
  </td>
