</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      AVRO-972 uses a method on JsonNode that was introduced with Jackson 1.6.0.  Unfortunately, Hadoop in a distributed environment places jackson on the mapreduce classpath prior to a user&#39;s Jar.<br/>
<br/>
Avro should function when this happens.<br/>
<br/>
There are two things we are using that are new in Jackson 1.6.0 -- JsonNode.getValueAsDouble()  and MinimalPrettyPrinter<br/>
<br/>
MinimalPrettyPrinter is OK because the class is new, and if there is a Jackson 1.5.x jar on a classpath before one that is &gt;= 1.6.0, it will find the class in the second jar.  We need to avoid JsonNode.getValueAsDouble() however.  There is a replacement that is equivalent and existed prior, JsonNode.getDoubleValue().<br/>

  </td>
