                                            <td class="description">      The avro_file_writer code in the C bindings allocate a large (64K) buffer on the stack.  This causes (very) hard-to-diagnose bugs if you try to output a data file from within a function with limited stack space.  (For instance, if you&#39;re running inside of a coroutine or thread with a 64K stack...)
