                <tr id="issuerow12553054" rel="12553054" data-issuekey="AVRO-1073" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1073" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1073">AVRO-1073</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                JSON encoder doesn&#39;t encode binary data properly
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Zhihong Zhang
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Zhihong Zhang
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/Apr/12 22:22 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 10/Sep/14 10:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.6.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      uname -a<br/>
Darwin zmac 10.8.0 Darwin Kernel Version 10.8.0: Tue Jun  7 16:33:36 PDT 2011; root:xnu-1504.15.3~1/RELEASE_I386 i386<br/>
<br/>
java -version<br/>
java version &quot;1.6.0_29&quot;<br/>
Java(TM) SE Runtime Environment (build 1.6.0_29-b11-402-10M3527)<br/>
Java HotSpot(TM) 64-Bit Server VM (build 20.4-b02-402, mixed mode)<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The JSON encoder doesn&#39;t encode binary data (bytes or ByteBuffer) properly. It treats the data as Latin-1 and encode it as text. But there is a bug in text encoding of non-Roman characters so the binary encoding doesn&#39;t work at all.<br/>
<br/>
The binary should be encoded into ASCII (Base64 or 85) before it&#39;s encoded in JSON. The text encoding of binary data is very inefficient even it works. For example, the 0 is encoded as &quot;\\u0000&quot; in JSON (7 bytes).
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
