</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m using avro Reflection API for a specific use case and I have a bug where if the object I&#39;m trying to get the Schema for has a field of type BigDecimal. Because BigDecimal extends java.lang.Number, we try to create a primitive schema for it but fail doing so with the following error:<br/>
<br/>
*{{org.apache.avro.AvroRuntimeException: Not a Specific class: class java.math.BigDecimal}}*<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;m attaching a unit test that shows the problem with a basic type that has a single BigDecimal field.<br/>
<br/>
This basically also applied to all subclasses of java.lang.Number that are not primitives.
