                <tr id="issuerow12607390" rel="12607390" data-issuekey="AVRO-1160" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1160" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1160">AVRO-1160</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Avro-C: avrocat can report read errors
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Lucas Martin-King
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Lucas Martin-King
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/Sep/12 03:05 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Sep/12 21:16 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 13/Sep/12 21:29 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.7.2            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        c            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently avrocat does not report any errors resulting from avro_file_reader_read_value().<br/>
<br/>
Currently avro_file_reader_read_value() doesn&#39;t report if we reach EOF, due to lower level error reporting limitations in Avro C. Instead, we check if we have reached EOF before reporting any errors. This is a bit rudimentary, however we at least get some indication of errors.<br/>
<br/>
I have reworked avrocat to always use avro_file_reader_fp().
  </td>
