                <tr id="issuerow12608089" rel="12608089" data-issuekey="AVRO-1168" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1168" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1168">AVRO-1168</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                IDL Tool - Field properties are added against schema instead of field
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Invalid
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Cristian Opris
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Cristian Opris
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Sep/12 16:34 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Sep/12 21:22 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 18/Sep/12 16:57 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In Idl.jj, field properties are added against the field *schema* instead of the field, resulting in an error if different fields of the same *record*<br/>
type are annotated with the same property name.<br/>
<br/>
Example:<br/>
&lt;code&gt;<br/>
record RecordA {<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
record RecordB {<br/>
 @Prop(&quot;&quot;)<br/>
 RecordA a1<br/>
<br/>
 @Prop(&quot;&quot;)<br/>
 RecordA a2<br/>
}<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Note this fails even if a1 and a2 are in different records (since the Schema instance is shared)<br/>
<br/>
Proposed fix: - change Idl.jj to add props agains the fields props, not the schema:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;code&gt;<br/>
    for (String key : props.keySet())<br/>
      type.addProp(key, getTextProp(key, props, token));<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
<br/>
should read:<br/>
&lt;code&gt;<br/>
 field.addProp(...)<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
