                <tr id="issuerow12614857" rel="12614857" data-issuekey="AVRO-1191" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1191" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1191">AVRO-1191</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                C++ json encoder uses \U instead of \u
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Keh-Li Sheng
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Keh-Li Sheng
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 05/Nov/12 21:41 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Jun/17 17:27 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        c++            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-1080                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      From the JSON spec http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc4627.txt:<br/>
<br/>
{quote}<br/>
2.5.  Strings<br/>
<br/>
   The representation of strings is similar to conventions used in the C<br/>
   family of programming languages.  A string begins and ends with<br/>
   quotation marks.  All Unicode characters may be placed within the<br/>
   quotation marks except for the characters that must be escaped:<br/>
   quotation mark, reverse solidus, and the control characters (U+0000<br/>
   through U+001F).<br/>
<br/>
   Any character may be escaped.  If the character is in the Basic<br/>
   Multilingual Plane (U+0000 through U+FFFF), then it may be<br/>
   represented as a six-character sequence: a reverse solidus, followed<br/>
   by the lowercase letter u, followed by four hexadecimal digits that<br/>
   encode the character&#39;s code point.  The hexadecimal letters A though<br/>
   F can be upper or lowercase.  So, for example, a string containing<br/>
   only a single reverse solidus character may be represented as<br/>
   &quot;\u005C&quot;.<br/>
{quote}<br/>
<br/>
But JsonCodec.cc outputs \U
  </td>
