                <tr id="issuerow12615299" rel="12615299" data-issuekey="AVRO-1199" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1199" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1199">AVRO-1199</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                SortedKeyValueFile$Writer.append method have a puzzle for the sorted key
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Doug Cutting
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Libing Sun
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Libing Sun
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Nov/12 07:32 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 10/Dec/12 17:57 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 14/Nov/12 23:21 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.7.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      At the SortedKeyValueFile.java 539 lines like next:<br/>
mPreviousKey = key;<br/>
<br/>
This class is same as Hadoop&#39;s MapFile, at the MapFile the same methon will keep a copy for this key, but not use &quot;=&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
If use &quot;=&quot; at here, when user append a reuse key object to this file. will cause key sorted not valid.<br/>
<br/>
I think next code will fix it:<br/>
<br/>
private DataInputBuffer inBuf = new DataInputBuffer();<br/>
private DataOutputBuffer outBuf = new DataOutputBuffer();<br/>
<br/>
      GenericDatumWriter&lt;K&gt; writer = new ReflectDatumWriter&lt;K&gt;(schema);<br/>
      GenericDatumReader&lt;K&gt; reader = new ReflectDatumReader&lt;K&gt;(schema);<br/>
      writer.write(key, encoder);<br/>
      inBuf.reset(outBuf.getData(), outBuf.getLength());<br/>
      BinaryDecoder decoder = DecoderFactory.get().directBinaryDecoder(inBuf,<br/>
          null);<br/>
      lastKey = reader.read(null, decoder); 
  </td>
