                <tr id="issuerow12616081" rel="12616081" data-issuekey="AVRO-1205" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1205" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1205">AVRO-1205</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Add Stereotype Annotation to Generated Beans
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sharmarke Aden
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Sharmarke Aden
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Sharmarke Aden
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 14/Nov/12 15:52 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 10/Dec/12 17:57 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 21/Nov/12 22:57 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.7.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Avro generated schema beans currently lack a formal way of distinguishing them as Avro schema beans at runtime. I would like to propose that a new stereotype annotation be added to Avro Core and the ability to have all Avro generated schema beans annotated with this newly created stereotype annotation.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;m planning on adding a FallbackTypeConverter to the Camel-Avro project and I hoping this feature will allow me to cleanly detect Avro beans for conversion at runtime.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
If this feature is implemented Avro schema beans would look something like this:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
...<br/>
<br/>
@org.apache.avro.reflect.AvroSchema<br/>
public class User extends org.apache.avro.specific.SpecificRecordBase implements org.apache.avro.specific.SpecificRecord {<br/>
<br/>
...<br/>
<br/>
}<br/>
...<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
The maven plugin configuration would look something like this:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
&lt;plugin&gt;<br/>
  &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.avro&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
  &lt;artifactId&gt;avro-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
  &lt;executions&gt;<br/>
    &lt;execution&gt;<br/>
      &lt;goals&gt;<br/>
        &lt;goal&gt;schema&lt;/goal&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/goals&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/execution&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/executions&gt;<br/>
  &lt;configuration&gt;<br/>
