                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The Ruby implementation of schema and protocol parsing violates the following statement in the Avro spec, with respect to name resolution: *&quot;the namespace is taken from the most tightly enclosing schema or protocol&quot;*. Currently, any nested named types without explicit namespace property are taken as being in the default namespace, not in the enclosing schema/protocol&#39;s namespace.
