                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The current implementations of the C# datum readers perform resolution of the reader and writer schema on every call to Read. In my tests this was causing it to perform poorly when reading a large number of records (slower than parsing the same data from delimited text files). It would be more efficient if the reader only needed to resolve the schemas once.
