</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ubuntu 12.10
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When I put values into a map, the values appear delayed with one cycle:<br/>
<br/>
// pseudo code<br/>
map = Map()<br/>
for (i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) {<br/>
   map.put(i, i)<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
// then map contains the following elements: {&quot;0&quot;: &quot;1&quot;, &quot;1&quot;: &quot;2&quot;, &quot;2&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;3&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;4&quot;: &quot;&quot;} <br/>
<br/>
I wrote a sample code, which demonstrates the bug. I hope I&#39;m not wrong. I have also problems with the reference counting: if I comment out the free() calls in the program, I get glibc errors. Is it possible, that the Avro frees not just its own pointers in the *decref() calls?
  </td>
