</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently C++ code generation generates single header file which inludes all the type definitions and encoding and decoding of the types. When generated header file is huge, we are experiencing issues when debugging in VS2010.<br/>
The issues are <br/>
1) Unable to set the breake point at desired location.<br/>
2) When compilation errors occur, doube click on an error taking the control to wrong location of the file.<br/>
<br/>
If split the file into mulitple parts, then it works. Is it possible to make the changes to codegeneration to do generate mulitple header files for type?<br/>

  </td>
