                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      all
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When you try to create an union comprising say an array of ints and an array of strings, you get a &quot;&quot;Duplicate in union: array&quot;.<br/>
I appreciate that this is in the spec, but the spec is wrong since an array of ints and an array of strings have different types.<br/>
Two ways to fix this:<br/>
 - provide support for named arrays<br/>
 - dig into array element type 
  </td>
