                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Following AVRO-1385, it appears Avro&#39;s resolving decoder performs decode-time compatibility check, ie. per datum instance compatibility check, as opposed to per schema compatibility check.<br/>
<br/>
For our use-cases, we need to determine whether all datum instances of a particular writer schema will always succeed in being decoded using a given reader schema.
