</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      There is no way to use compression with the C++ DataFileReader and C++ DataFileWriter, from what I can tell. Adding compression of the written blocks using boost streams is relatively straight forward and I can provide a patch if people are interested. <br/>
<br/>
However, there are a couple caveats:<br/>
- the windows builds of boost don&#39;t currently include zlib support (required for compression) by default. You have to do extra work to get it.<br/>
- I don&#39;t know if doing it that way is compatible with other avro implementations
  </td>
