                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      A common Avro mistake is to declare optional fields as follows:<br/>
<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
&quot;type&quot;: [&quot;string&quot;, &quot;null&quot;], &quot;default&quot;: null<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
This fails at runtime since the default value&#39;s type (null) doesn&#39;t match the type of the first type in the union (string). The correct declaration is:<br/>
<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
&quot;type&quot;: [&quot;null&quot;, &quot;string&quot;], &quot;default&quot;: null<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
Doug [suggested|https://groups.google.com/a/cloudera.org/forum/#!msg/cdk-dev/Xgo5YKEcQ1Q/VkyWP2gnOEMJ] that we throw an exception at schema parse time for cases like this. To ensure backwards compatibility we could make it optional; tools could emit a warning.
  </td>
