</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When serializing a record with a field that isn&#39;t specified in the schema, there should be some sort of warning or error. Otherwise, a simple typo in a field name can lead to silent loss of that field&#39;s data.<br/>
<br/>
Test case that should pass but currently fails:<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
{<br/>
    my $schema = Avro::Schema-&gt;parse(&lt;&lt;EOJ);<br/>
          {<br/>
          &quot;type&quot;: &quot;record&quot;,<br/>
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;test&quot;,<br/>
          &quot;fields&quot; : [<br/>
          {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;a&quot;, &quot;type&quot;: &quot;long&quot;}<br/>
          ]<br/>
          }<br/>
EOJ<br/>
    my $enc = &#39;&#39;;<br/>
    eval {<br/>
        Avro::BinaryEncoder-&gt;encode(<br/>
            schema =&gt; $schema,<br/>
            data =&gt; { a =&gt; 27, b =&gt; &#39;foo&#39; },<br/>
            emit_cb =&gt; sub { $enc .= ${ $_[0] } },<br/>
        );<br/>
    };<br/>
    isa_ok $@, &#39;Avro::BinaryEncoder::Error&#39;;<br/>
}<br/>
{noformat}
  </td>
