                <tr id="issuerow12699849" rel="12699849" data-issuekey="AVRO-1480" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1480" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1480">AVRO-1480</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                AvroTypeException should include fieldName as distinct field
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Will Sargent
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Will Sargent
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 10/Mar/14 20:06 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 12/Mar/14 19:29 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.6            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
Currently AvroTypeException is defined as <br/>
<br/>
public class AvroTypeException extends AvroRuntimeException {<br/>
  public AvroTypeException(String message) { super(message); }<br/>
  public AvroTypeException(String message, Throwable cause) {<br/>
    super(message, cause);<br/>
  }<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
And when used in JSONDecoder, field name failures are defined like this:<br/>
<br/>
throw new AvroTypeException(&quot;Expected field name not found: &quot; + fa.fname);<br/>
<br/>
This means that, in the event of an AvroTypeException, the only way to find which field has the error is to scan through the error message.<br/>
<br/>
If the AvroTypeException had a constructor (message, throwable, field) or a subclass which explicitly provided fields, then it would make error processing much easier.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
