                <tr id="issuerow12718277" rel="12718277" data-issuekey="AVRO-1523" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1523" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1523">AVRO-1523</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Perl API: int/long type minimum value checks are off by one
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Patch Available
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            John Karp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            John Karp
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            John Karp
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 03/Jun/14 23:37 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 24/Jul/14 20:14 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.7.8            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        perl            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      -2,147,483,648 is rejected as an int, and −9,223,372,036,854,775,808 is rejected as a long when passed to the binary encoder, but they are valid signed 32-bit and 64-bit numbers respectively.<br/>
<br/>
The problem is that the range check is made against the absolute value of the input, but in two&#39;s complement arithmetic types the minimum and maximum values have different absolute values.<br/>

  </td>
