                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Instead of having to provide an already compiled schema, there should be the ability to generate the schema from a java object. <br/>
That is because in some case, providing the schema is not posssible  (e.g: the class of that Java Object has some members whose types are external java classes in external libraries or simply the Object is too complex).<br/>
<br/>
Example of how it would be:<br/>
{{Shema schema = new Schema.Parser.parse(T);}}<br/>
<br/>
Microsoft already implemented this feature in its Avro library for .NET so I was surprised that it wasn&#39;t already implemented. 
  </td>
