                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      - Ruby 1.8 is EOL, and is even security issues aren&#39;t addressed anymore. <br/>
- It is also getting hard to set up Ruby 1.8 to run the tests (e.g. on a recent OSX, it won&#39;t compile without manual fiddling).<br/>
- Handling character encodings in Ruby 1.9 is very different than Ruby 1.8. Supporting both at the same time adds a lot of overhead.
