                <tr id="issuerow12757617" rel="12757617" data-issuekey="AVRO-1610" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1610" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1610">AVRO-1610</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                HttpTransceiver.java allocates arbitrary amount of memory
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Philip Zeyliger
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Philip Zeyliger
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Nov/14 05:49 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 01/Sep/16 21:19 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.7            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In {{HttpTransceiver.java}}, Avro does:<br/>
{code}<br/>
      int length = (in.read()&lt;&lt;24)+(in.read()&lt;&lt;16)+(in.read()&lt;&lt;8)+in.read();<br/>
      if (length == 0) {                       // end of buffers<br/>
        return buffers;<br/>
      }<br/>
      ByteBuffer buffer = ByteBuffer.allocate(length);<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
This means that badly formatted input (like that produced by {{curl http://host/ --data foo}} and many common security scanners) will trigger an OutOfMemory exception.  This is undesirable, especially combined with setups that kill the process on out of memory exceptions.<br/>
<br/>
This bug is similar in spirit to AVRO-1111.
  </td>
