</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Quite often, when I declare mapreduce jobs I have to create the union of two or three schemas. For example:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
AvroJob.setMapOutputKeySchema(job, Schema.createUnion(Arrays.asList(Foo.SCHEMA$, Bar.SCHEMA$))<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
Having Schema.createUnion only accept a List hurts readability and force users to write boilerplate code for such trivial, but I believe common, use cases. It would be create to add {{Schema.createUnion(Schema... type)}} 
  </td>
