</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The NettyServer constructor adds a new instance of NettyServerAvroHandler to the ChannelPipeline. For those who&#39;d like to provide their own handler (by extending NettyServerAvroHandler or ChannelUpstreamHandler) a protected &quot;createNettyServerAvroHandler&quot; method can instead be called. This will allow sub classes of NettyServer to provide their own handler. <br/>
<br/>
This follows the same pattern found in NettyTransceiver, where the protected &quot;createNettyClientAvroHandler&quot; method is called when creating the ChannelPipeline.
  </td>
