                <tr id="issuerow12860688" rel="12860688" data-issuekey="AVRO-1723" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1723" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1723">AVRO-1723</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Add support for forward declarations in avro IDL
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Zoltan Farkas
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Zoltan Farkas
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Zoltan Farkas
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 31/Aug/15 14:17 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/May/17 17:15 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 19/May/17 17:15 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.8.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">7</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-1667,                                                AVRO-1997                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently Recursive data structures like:<br/>
<br/>
record SampleNode {<br/>
   int count = 0;<br/>
   array&lt;SamplePair&gt; samples = [];<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
record SamplePair {<br/>
 string name;<br/>
 SampleNode node;<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
It is not possible to declare in IDL,<br/>
however it is possible to declare in avsc (with fix from https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1667 )<br/>
<br/>
It is actually not complicated to implement, here is some detail on a possible implementation:<br/>
<br/>
https://github.com/zolyfarkas/avro/commit/210c50105717149f3daa39b8d4160b8548b8e363<br/>
<br/>
This would close a capability gap with google protocol buffers...
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310220">            <span title="10/Sep/15 17:28"><time class="livestamp allow-future" datetime="2015-09-10T17:28:13+0000">10/Sep/15 5:28 PM</time></span>
    </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312322"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312520"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312323"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312521">    6 weeks, 5 days ago

                        </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312320"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310420">      9223372036854775807
  </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312321"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312120">
</td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312121"><span class="sla-agent-restricted">Restricted to agents</span>
</td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312328"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312329"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312923"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312326"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312920"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312327"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312921"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312720"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312324"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312325"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310192">      With this patch recursive data structures will be supported in IDL:<br/>
<br/>
record SampleNode {<br/>
  int count = 0;<br/>
  array&lt;SamplePair&gt; samples = []; <br/>
}<br/>
record SamplePair {<br/>
 string name;<br/>
 SampleNode node; <br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
Also the order of declaration of named types will not matter anymore. (similar with other languages like java)<br/>
<br/>
Compatibility: <br/>
<br/>
All schemas that are compilable with older versions of AVRO will continue working without issues.<br/>
IDLs that will take advantage of the the features introduced with this patch, will not be compilable with older versions of AVRO<br/>
please see the dependent JIRAs for more detail on related issues.
  </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310191">


</td>
