                <tr id="issuerow12895774" rel="12895774" data-issuekey="AVRO-1742" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1742" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1742">AVRO-1742</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Avro C# DataFileWriter Flush() does not flush the buffer to disk
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Mika Ristimaki
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Mika Ristimaki
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Sep/15 13:10 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Sep/15 13:10 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In C# DataFileWriter.Flush() is implemented as <br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
public void Flush()<br/>
        {<br/>
            EnsureHeader();<br/>
            Sync();<br/>
        }<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
Is this by Avro spec or is this a bug. So should calling DataFileWriter.Flush() just start a new Sync block  and not flush the file to disc?<br/>
<br/>
In Java the implementation is<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
 @Override<br/>
  public void flush() throws IOException {<br/>
    sync();<br/>
    vout.flush();<br/>
  }<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
where vout is a BinaryEncoder. So I think the correct implementation in C# is<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
public void Flush()<br/>
        {<br/>
            EnsureHeader();<br/>
            Sync();<br/>
           _encoder.Flush()<br/>
        }<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
If someone can confirm my suspicion I&#39;ll try to contribute a fix in the near future.<br/>
<br/>

