</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The docker image includes node.js version 0.10.29, which is too old to run the current set of JS unit tests. The latest stable version is 5.1.0 and the &quot;mature and dependable&quot; version is 4.2.2, so the version in docker (from ubuntu) is quite old. The install instructions for 4.2.2 aren&#39;t very difficult:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
curl -sL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_4.x | sudo -E bash -<br/>
sudo apt-get install -y nodejs<br/>
{code}
