                <tr id="issuerow12957725" rel="12957725" data-issuekey="AVRO-1827" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1827" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1827">AVRO-1827</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Handling correctly optional fields when converting Protobuf to Avro
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jakub Kahovec
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jakub Kahovec
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 11/Apr/16 14:47 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 02/Nov/16 16:07 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.7,                     1.8.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">2</td>
                                            <td class="watches">6</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hello,<br/>
as of the current implementation of converting protobuf files into avro format, protobuf optional fields are being  given default values in the avro schema if not specified explicitly. <br/>
So for instance when the protobuf field is defined as  <br/>
{quote}<br/>
optional int64 fieldInt64 = 1;<br/>
{quote}<br/>
in the avro schema it appears as<br/>
{quote}<br/>
 &quot;name&quot; : &quot;fieldInt64&quot;,<br/>
  &quot;type&quot; : &quot;long&quot;,<br/>
  &quot;default&quot; : 0<br/>
{quote}<br/>
The problem with this implementation is that we are losing information about whether the field was present or not in the original protobuf, as when we ask for this field&#39;s value in avro we will be given the default value. <br/>
<br/>
What I&#39;m proposing instead is that if the field in the protobuf is defined as optional and has no default value then the generated avro schema type will us a union comprising the matching type and null type with default value null. It is going to look like this:<br/>
{quote}<br/>
 &quot;name&quot; : &quot;fieldIn64&quot;,<br/>
  &quot;type&quot; : [ &quot;null&quot;, &quot;long&quot; ],<br/>
  &quot;default&quot; : null<br/>
{quote}<br/>
I&#39;m aware that is a breaking change but I think that is the proper way how to handle optional fields.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve also  created a patch which fixes the conversion<br/>
<br/>
Jakub <br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
