                <tr id="issuerow12971680" rel="12971680" data-issuekey="AVRO-1849" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1849" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1849">AVRO-1849</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                C++ printJson fails on record with no fields
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Simon Woodford
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Simon Woodford
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Simon Woodford
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 20/May/16 22:03 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 28/Sep/16 12:39 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 27/Sep/16 14:54 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.7,                     1.8.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.9.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        c++            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">4</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Not relevant
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The function NodeRecord::printJson in lang/c++/impl/NodeImpl.cc does not correctly handle a record with no fields. It injects an extra closing curly brace, and the result is invalid JSON. <br/>
Starting with a schema<br/>
{<br/>
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;record&quot;, <br/>
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Example&quot;,<br/>
  &quot;fields&quot; : [<br/>
  ]<br/>
}<br/>
and parsing it to create a ValidSchema, then calling toJson on the ValidSchema generates<br/>
{<br/>
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;record&quot;, <br/>
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Example&quot;,<br/>
  &quot;fields&quot; : [<br/>
    }<br/>
  ]<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
A record with no fields is unusual but we have encountered use cases for it, avro does not invalidate a record with no fields, and I&#39;ve confirmed that Java, C and C# handle this case correctly. (I have not checked the other supported languages.)<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
