                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The JSON encodeNumber(double) function writes value to output string stream. The default precision is 6 which is not sufficient for many applications for encoding a double.<br/>
<br/>
std::setprecision(16) should be used to set max precision to 16 digits. Note that doing this would not unnecessarily append zeros to force 16 digits.
