                for avro HTTP content type instead of avro/binary, application/octet-stream;fmt=avro might be more appropriate?
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Zoltan Farkas
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Zoltan Farkas
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Sep/16 20:25 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Sep/16 20:25 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      the content type is defined in:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
/** An HTTP-based {@link Transceiver} implementation. */<br/>
public class HttpTransceiver extends Transceiver {<br/>
  static final String CONTENT_TYPE = &quot;avro/binary&quot;;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
I suggest using for avro binary:<br/>
application/octet-stream;fmt=avro<br/>
and for avro json:<br/>
application/json;fmt=avro<br/>
<br/>
this would take advantage of standard mime types...<br/>

  </td>
