                <tr id="issuerow13006984" rel="13006984" data-issuekey="AVRO-1925" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1925" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1925">AVRO-1925</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Docker clash with SELinux
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Simon Woodford
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Simon Woodford
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 22/Sep/16 23:34 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 22/Sep/16 23:34 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.8.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.8.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        docker            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Linux - Centos 7 with SELinux running, avro found in /home/&lt;username&gt;. 
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When Docker is running in a labelling system like SELinux, it needs to be told to relabel any directories it wants to write to. <br/>
In build.sh, we tell Docker that it can access /home/USER_NAME, /home/.m2 and /home/.gnupg, but we don&#39;t instruct it to relabel them. So if SELinux is running, once in the docker container, you cannot build anything as that involves writing. <br/>
See e.g. the Volume Labels section in https://docs.docker.com/engine/tutorials/dockervolumes/ for more details. 
  </td>
