                <tr id="issuerow13011653" rel="13011653" data-issuekey="AVRO-1933" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Avro
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="AVRO-1933" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/AVRO-1933">AVRO-1933</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                SchemaCompatibility class could be more user-friendly about incompatibilities
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Patch Available
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Anders Sundelin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Anders Sundelin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Oct/16 12:40 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 02/Mar/17 12:23 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.7.7,                     1.8.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.9.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        java            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">3</td>
                                            <td class="watches">7</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate">3600</td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate">3600</td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">            0%
    </td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        AVRO-2003                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Any Java env
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Today, the class SchemaCompatibility reports incompatibilities with quite little detail. The whole reader and the whole writer schema is listed, and no particular detail about what was incompatible.<br/>
<br/>
The attached patch fixes this, introducing a new enum (SchemaIncompatibilityType), and more specific sub-schemas that were incompatible.<br/>
The old, overall picture, is still there - the new compatibility state is encapsulated in the SchemaCompatibilityDetails class.<br/>
Lots of test cases have been added, and there has been refactoring done in the TestSchemaCompatibility and other test classes.<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     0%
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     0%
</td>
