</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                avrogencpp: unlike java, c++ generated code doesn&#39;t include own schema
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Alexander Moriarty
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Alexander Moriarty
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Oct/16 10:10 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Nov/16 11:08 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.8.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        c++            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      All the classes generated for java include a copy of their schema. The C++ classes do not.<br/>
<br/>
Every generated java class has getClassSchema().<br/>
Something similar for C++ would be convenient.<br/>
<br/>
During generation, the schema is available with n-&gt;printJson(..) which can then be passed through boost::algorithm::erase_all() to remove whitespace and new lines, and then boost::algorithm::replace_all() to add escape characters back.<br/>
and then given to avro::compileJsonSchemaFromString<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
